WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.150
It’s probably this.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.010
Where am I?  Who am I?

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.560
You're finally back.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:16.200
Oh yeah.  I ate a bad program.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.130
You're a glutton.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.480
Kusanagi!  You’re back?

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.240
Yeah.  Nothing I can do from there.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.310
I came here to find the culprit.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.950
What happened?

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:39.570
He stole my brother’s 
consciousness in front of me.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:42.060
Why your brother, Kusanagi?

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.390
I don’t know.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:47.140
But to digitize and steal a 
person’s consciousness…

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.940
That’s far more impressive 
than Hanoi's computer virus.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:57.470
That’s right!  The new enemy is formidable!

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:58.710
Yeah…

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.170
A new enemy…

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:06.020
I promise to find him and retrieve 
your brother’s consciousness!

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:30.220
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:37.030
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:44.340
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:50.910
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:57.650
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:04.890
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:11.600
I want to share your pain

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.640
Brother, kneel.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.880
Did you acquire Jin Kusanagi’s data?

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.940
Yes, but we faced an unexpected enemy.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.040
An unexpected enemy?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.910
Playmaker.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.880
So Playmaker came back to LINK VRAINS.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.690
Yes, along with the Dark Ignis.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:24.110
We lost the duel, but Bohman 
gained some experience.

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:26.230
There's something more important.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:27.830
What is it?

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.520
Another Ignis appeared.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.300
It was Fire Attribute.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.590
I see.  I anticipated that.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:39.800
Bit and Boot tried to 
capture it, but they lost.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.270
They'll eventually find this place.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.630
We need to prepare.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:48.810
But before that, hand over 
Jin Kusanagi’s data.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:50.760
Bohman…

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:05.320
Now as you promised, return our memories.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.160
I never made that promise.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.540
What?

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:14.190
You only think such a promise exists.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.680
I’ll reset your memories.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.550
He requires new memories again.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:23.480
Yes.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.480
Roboppi is happy!

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.190
You're back!

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:35.080
When you returned to your homeworld, 
I thought you abandoned me!

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.680
Don't be silly!

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:39.800
I would never abandon you and go home.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.390
You’re right!

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:45.820
Because you promised to make me smarter!

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:50.350
Exactly!  You’re my precious minion!

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.440
Roboopi wants to become smarter!

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.020
Leave it to me!

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:58.380
If you do as I say, you'll 
be smart in no time.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:02.880
By the way, who’s that 
you're snuggling with?

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.820
This is Linkuriboh.  My minion.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:11.150
Minion?  You mean Roboppi’s rival?

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.560
It’s hard being a popular AI.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:23.140
Haven’t been to school in a while.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:26.510
Lots of people who look alike.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:28.730
Don’t risk getting found.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:30.220
I know.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:33.850
But why did you lock me up again?

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:39.850
#1: Kusanagi is emotionally hurt because 
his brother’s consciousness was stolen.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:44.240
It's good to have someone he can 
talk to who knows our situation.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.960
Are you saying I’m a friend?

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:48.200
Not bad.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:55.140
#2: The attacks on your homeworld 
and Kusanagi's brother trouble me.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:58.940
And their teammates wanted an Ignis.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:03.040
You may be linked to this incident.

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:04.510
Me?

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.750
#3: And this is the most important.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.430
What?

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.730
Being a hostage suits you.

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:15.420
Oh.  Zing.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:29.670
So that’s Blue Angel.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:33.680
Hey Zaizen, the club'll 
meet in the AV room today.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:34.640
Okay.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:39.750
No one seems to know she’s 
LINK VRAINS’s idol.

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:45.350
By the way, the other one is Brave 
Max, aka Playmaker’s best friend.

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:47.580
I don’t care.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:52.430
And that’s Playmaker.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.370
How should I approach him…

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.380
That was close.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.740
Why did he suddenly look my way?

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.310
No need to be sneaky.

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:07.550
He recognized us.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:10.940
But I just transferred!

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:14.180
I recently contacted the Dark Ignis.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:16.920
Hey!  Stop doing stuff on your own!

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:22.160
Since he's hiding his identity, 
he'll be wary of that message.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.620
No need to worry about that too.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:29.640
Unlike humans, the Ignis don’t 
communicate using simple language.

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:33.490
We use high level code 
that humans can't decode.

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:37.170
The Dark Ignis won't distrust me.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:38.540
But still-

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:41.920
I said there’s no need for lame tricks.

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:46.600
They're heroes that defeated the 
Knights of Hanoi and saved the world.

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:48.900
They’re not shut-ins like you.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.650
I fought too!

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:52.240
With yourself.

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:56.390
But they went beyond and fought enemies.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.420
Be quiet!

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:02.030
It's childish to get upset when 
I hit the nail on the head.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:03.520
You should stop doing that.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:04.630
Anyway, here he comes.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.840
Hey, Playmaker…

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.750
Who are you?

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:14.180
How do you know my identity?

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:16.030
I’ll tell you soon enough.

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:18.640
We met yesterday.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:21.020
I’m Soulburner.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:23.480
You’re Soulburner?

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:26.220
My name is Takeru Homura.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:29.090
He’s the one who saved you?

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.230
What are you after?

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:34.830
Don’t get the wrong idea.  I’m your ally.

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:36.570
I’ll show you proof.

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:40.210
And why I know your identity.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.810
Ignis!

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.900
So it was you!

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:47.910
We meet for the first time, Playmaker.

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:51.460
In this world, they call me Flame.

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:54.420
No, you named yourself.

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:58.500
My name in kanji means "indomitable 
soul dream."  Pronounced "Flame."

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:01.390
Unlike someone’s cutesy name, it’s cool.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.760
Who you referring to?

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:05.790
Long time no see.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:08.720
In this world, I heard you’re called Ai.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:10.600
You can call me that too!

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:12.380
That Ignis is…

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:15.680
As its name says, it's Fire Attribute.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.800
It’s an AI based on me.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.340
Then you too?

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:22.350
I’m also a victim of the Lost Incident.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:27.780
He arrived after the Tower of Hanoi, 
and I learned what happened to me.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:32.430
The Hanoi are gone.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:36.620
But the Cyberse World was attacked.  
There's a new incident.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:41.330
So we decided to confront my life together.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.290
A new incident…

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:48.930
By the way!  Flame, you know what 
happened to Cyberse World, right?

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:54.010
Let’s change locations.  This 
isn’t the right place to talk.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:58.610
What a nice view!

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.680
An unbroken view of Den City!

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.650
This is a place fitting for 
a serious conversation?

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:08.660
No one can eavesdrop here.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:11.090
A huge wheel that spins in the sky.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.440
We should've built one in Cyberse World.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.530
You just wanted to ride this.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:19.500
Flame, no more joking.  Tell us.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:23.440
Fine.  This is what happened.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:30.500
Ai, we held many discussions 
after you hid Cyberse World.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:33.520
Discussions?  About what?

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:39.370
The Ignis created technology 
superior to the human world's.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:44.630
We discussed whether to trust humans and 
give our technology so we can live together.

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:47.560
Your technology is that great?

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.180
You'll never know.  Your net skills stink.

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:52.440
You always diss me.

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:54.300
I’m only telling the truth.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.530
Whatever.  Continue.

00:10:56.530 --> 00:11:01.680
Our creator, Dr. Kogami, tried to kill us.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.620
Even his son Revolver.

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:09.280
That proved humans had the 
potential to become our enemy.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:11.060
Revolver said…

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:17.360
AI will begin to control people, and 
people will view AI as the enemy.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:21.340
That will cause AI to 
view humans as the enemy.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:27.630
How ironic that Dr. Kogami was the cause.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:31.820
But we didn’t reach a final conclusion.

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:35.630
We were examining many 
different possibilities.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:39.140
That's when a new enemy attacked.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.120
A new enemy?

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:47.520
The enemy knew our weaknesses and 
destroyed Cyberse World instantly.

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:51.110
The enemy broke through my program?

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:54.260
You created a really lame program.

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:56.790
It was not lame!

00:11:56.790 --> 00:12:00.720
It was the best I could create at the time!

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:03.860
It's true...

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:07.240
Flame, who's the new enemy?

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.540
I can’t even guess.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:11.110
Not the Hanoi?

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:13.370
That's unlikely.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:17.980
When the new enemy arrived, you 
were still fighting the Hanoi.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:19.640
I see...

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:23.560
We barely escaped Cyberse World alive.

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:25.980
What happened to the other four?

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:28.590
I'm searching for them!

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:29.820
I see...

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:32.700
There are six total Ignis.

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:37.060
Yeah.  Like Duel Monsters, 
there are six Attributes.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.300
What's Kusanagi’s brother’s Attribute?

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:42.790
Only the Ignis paired with him knows.

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:45.040
Because we don’t need that info.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:49.050
I never believed I'd contact Yusei.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:55.390
Due to the current situation, and to create 
a safe location isolated from the net...

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:57.890
...I contacted Takeru for the first time.

00:12:57.890 --> 00:13:01.400
Ai, let’s search for the others together.

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.080
Yeah!  Sure!

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:06.000
Playmaker, will you help us too?

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:11.740
I understand how you feel, but I have 
to search for Kusanagi’s brother.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:14.060
That's no problem.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:16.140
The two incidents are linked.

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:18.010
How so?

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:22.390
The Link Spell that our opponents used.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:27.080
Those who attacked Cyberse 
World also used that card.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:30.730
What?

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:36.260
Kusanagi’s brother's kidnappers and those 
who attacked Cyberse World are the same?

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:37.700
High probability.

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:41.440
Then our priority is to 
find the escaped duelist.

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:44.220
Where did they go?

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:48.680
Let’s ask Kusanagi.  He should 
be analyzing that duelist.

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:52.040
But isn’t Kusanagi depressed?

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.200
Kusanagi is tough.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.790
He never loses sight of what must be done.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:02.390
Then let’s get out of this filthy gondola.

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:05.390
You don't get to say that!

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:11.700
All the bounty hunters are finally here.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:14.300
I'll introduce them, Mr. Onizuka.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:17.300
Enough with the "Mister."

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:19.770
I’m always Go Onizuka.

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:23.380
Go Onizuka, he's Blood Shepherd.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:27.980
I was wondering who you'd be, 
but I never expected a mummy.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:32.760
I don’t get people who show 
their real face on the net.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:36.690
Revealing your identity 
on the net is a demerit.

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:41.190
I don’t care about that.  
But I’ll say one thing.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.290
I’ll be the one to defeat Playmaker!

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:45.220
You have a grudge against him?

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:47.820
He’s always ahead of me.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.040
I don’t like that!

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:51.260
I have no interest in that.

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:54.360
But I’ll also say one thing.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:56.560
Don’t order me around.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:59.020
I’ll do things my way.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:01.750
Is this okay, Chief?

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:04.800
I don’t think those two will get along.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.720
I never expected them to.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:15.350
Anyway, do you know who battled Playmaker?

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:19.100
If you do, it'll help track down Playmaker.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:20.260
Look at this.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:25.640
I continue to analyze it.

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:29.740
But unfortunately, we 
haven't found a lead yet.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:31.980
Where did he vanish to?

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:34.720
There's no record of him logging out.

00:15:35.020 --> 00:15:36.580
How did you know?

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.830
Even I can get that level of info.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.570
He vanished in LINK VRAINS's restricted area.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:46.530
Restricted area?

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:54.970
This wasn't neccessary.

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:58.840
It's fine.  I don’t have 
much to do these days.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:04.580
But I’m surprised Yusaku brought a friend.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:08.370
And that he knows our identities.

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:11.050
Yusaku told me the highlights.

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:13.560
Welcome, Homura and Flame.

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:17.400
Don’t worry.  I'll keep it a secret.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:19.560
I’m also a victim of the incident.

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:22.800
So I know what your brother went through.

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:27.300
I see.  You also had a rough time.

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:31.800
Please find the ones who stole 
my brother’s consciousness.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:35.610
As we let time pass by, 
what's happening to Jin…

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:37.730
I'll do whatever I can to help.

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.890
If there’s anything I can do, just ask.

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:45.050
He looks soft, but his core is strong.

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:48.720
He can sorta duel, so he can be helpful.

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:51.330
He thinks he's better than me?

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:55.030
Kusanagi, have you found a lead?

00:16:55.030 --> 00:17:01.940
Yusaku, your opponents vanished in 
LINK VRAINS’s restricted area.

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.280
Around here.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:10.640
Does that mean SOL Technologies 
is involved in this incident?

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:12.040
I don’t know.

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:15.130
But there’s certainly something there.

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:20.890
After checking the surrounding area, 
I found a shred of an unknown program.

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:22.830
This.

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:25.150
What is that?

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:27.460
This isn't my expertise.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:29.100
Do you know, Fujiki?

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:31.470
Don’t call him Fujiki.

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:33.260
Yusaku is fine.  Right?

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:34.240
I don’t mind.

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:37.070
Then call me Takeru.

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:41.640
I've never seen this program, but...

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:45.550
It’s similar to a program 
in Ai’s memories.

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:47.940
This is…

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:49.780
An Ignis program.

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:51.290
What?

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:53.020
It's Wind Attribute.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:55.490
There’s a Wind Ignis there?

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:57.860
Maybe, maybe not.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:02.470
Either way, we need to check that area.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:07.360
Thank you.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:11.050
Good day.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.270
Brother.

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:20.520
Thanks for waiting.

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:25.890
I never thought the day would come 
when the three of us would meet.

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:30.620
What did you want to talk 
to us about, brother?

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:41.750
Be careful.  Security 
camera ahead on the left.

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:42.670
Okay.

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:58.050
Are you able to transmit to Kusanagi?

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:01.930
Yeah.  I’m sending everything I see.

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:08.330
Kusanagi, learn anything?

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.520
No, nothing of note.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:11.800
So no good.

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:14.270
But something interesting came.

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:17.000
What?  Something interesting?

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:21.420
This is…

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:23.570
It's Ghost Girl!

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:26.650
It's info about the restricted area.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:28.880
And how to enter the area.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:30.980
Why did she send that?

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:33.990
She want us to go to that area?

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:36.410
Don’t!  It’s a trap!

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:39.290
She’s trying to trick us again!

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:46.240
It says a gate appeared in the restricted 
area that SOL Technologies hasn’t identified.

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:50.210
A gate?  That's where he went?

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.120
No no no!

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.810
You want to suffer again?

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:57.490
But this info seems real.

00:19:57.490 --> 00:20:00.920
You can only get this info 
from SOL Technologies.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.910
So Zaizen is the source?

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:09.720
Zaizen wants you to go 
through the gate and search.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:10.860
Exactly.

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:14.700
But SOL Technologies have bounty hunters.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:18.570
If you think about it, Ai 
is correct.  It’s a trap.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:21.110
Yes!  Definitely a trap!

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:24.660
But we have no other lead.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:28.150
Only that he vanished in that area.

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:32.120
Even if it’s a trap, we need 
to investigate that gate.

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:33.850
It’s dangerous.

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:35.210
Yeah!

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:36.220
I know.

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:41.160
Then let’s be fair!  Decide by majority!

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:43.320
Who’s against going?  Me!

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:45.290
It’s decided.

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:49.530
Fail!

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:53.690
What’s this program?

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:59.740
It’s a trap evasion program that Ghost 
Girl taught me and an updated LVSS.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:03.960
If it's a simple trap, the evasion 
program’s stealth function activates.

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:09.220
I added a communication function and an 
emergency escape program to the LVSS.

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:12.380
But you can only escape once.

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:14.590
Use it when you have no other choice.

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:16.320
Understood.

00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:18.060
Be careful.

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:19.200
Yeah.

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:24.870
Start stealth program.

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:43.230
Ghost Girl really wants us to go to the gate.

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:45.190
Not necessarily.

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:50.530
Playmaker!  Found you!

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:52.800
I told you so.

00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:54.900
Let’s go!  We’ll shake them off!

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:26.210
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:32.920
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:33.380 --> 00:22:36.420
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:39.560
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:40.020 --> 00:22:44.160
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:44.450 --> 00:22:47.130
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:51.860 --> 00:22:58.010
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:58.170 --> 00:23:01.150
With repeating "nows"

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:05.080
What about you?  "Live for now"

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:11.060
Grab the Shooting Star in 
the sky with both your hands

00:23:11.210 --> 00:23:14.330
Overcome "now" with all your might  Yell!

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:40.600
Onizuka's pride was completely destroyed.

00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:47.070
Since he had complete confidence in his 
power, he temporarily lost the will to fight.

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:53.240
Even if he has to give up his status and 
honor, there's someone he must defeat.

00:23:53.240 --> 00:23:56.400
In order to rediscover himself.

00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:59.030
I don't have time to take you on!

00:23:59.030 --> 00:24:02.620
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Man Who Gave Up Charisma

00:24:02.620 --> 00:24:04.800
Into the VRAINS!
